-Retrieval must distinguish a usable current state from unresolved review work. Exactly how those states are represented remains part of the open choice.
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Concurrent-edit policy | Whole-visit revisions: competing complete revisions, coordinator selects | Field-aware three-way merge; last-write-wins overwrite | Maintained merge rules can combine scientifically related edits — e.g., one worker's identification fix with another worker's cover estimate taken under the old identification — without anyone noticing. The team accepts a larger review volume as the cost of never auto-combining. Last-write-wins silently discards a submitted edit. Full tradeoffs and re-run conditions: decisions/concurrent-edit-policy.md |
